---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe34.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Basic Earnings Per Share" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Weighted Average Shares Outstanding" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Diluted Earnings Per Share" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. The If-Converted and Treasury Stock Methods" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Anti-Dilutive Instruments — Excluded From the Calculation" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — Calculating Basic EPS" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Calculating Diluted EPS With Convertible Bonds" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IAS 33" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A standardised profitability measure per ordinary share</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 34 governs the CALCULATION and PRESENTATION of EARNINGS PER SHARE (EPS) — a WIDELY-used, STANDARDISED measure of an ENTERPRISE'S profitability ON A PER-SHARE basis, ENABLING comparability BETWEEN companies and OVER time. THE Standard is CLOSELY converged with IAS 33 internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Companies with publicly traded ordinary shares</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to ENTERPRISES whose ORDINARY shares (or POTENTIAL ordinary SHARES) are PUBLICLY traded, REQUIRING the PRESENTATION of BOTH basic and DILUTED earnings PER share ON the FACE of the INCOME Statement.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Basic Earnings Per Share</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Profit attributable to ordinary shareholders, divided by weighted average shares</div><div class="text-supporting">BASIC EPS = PROFIT attributable to ORDINARY shareholders OF the parent (AFTER deducting PREFERENCE dividends) ÷ WEIGHTED average NUMBER of ORDINARY shares OUTSTANDING during the PERIOD.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Weighted Average Shares Outstanding</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Time-weighted for shares issued or repurchased during the period</div><div class="text-supporting">SHARES ISSUED or REPURCHASED DURING the period are WEIGHTED by the PROPORTION of the period THEY were OUTSTANDING — ENSURING the DENOMINATOR REFLECTS the ACTUAL capital AVAILABLE to GENERATE the reported PROFIT OVER time.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Diluted Earnings Per Share</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Adjusting for the potential dilutive effect of convertible instruments</div><div class="text-supporting">DILUTED EPS ADJUSTS the BASIC EPS calculation for the POTENTIAL dilutive EFFECT of CONVERTIBLE bonds, SHARE options, WARRANTS, and OTHER potential ORDINARY shares — SHOWING the LOWEST possible EPS figure that COULD result IF all DILUTIVE potential SHARES were CONVERTED or EXERCISED.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>The If-Converted and Treasury Stock Methods</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Adjusting both numerator and denominator</div><div class="text-supporting">FOR CONVERTIBLE instruments (e.g. CONVERTIBLE bonds), the "IF-CONVERTED" method ADDS BACK the AFTER-tax interest SAVED (had CONVERSION occurred) to the NUMERATOR, and ADDS the RESULTING additional SHARES to the DENOMINATOR. FOR OPTIONS and WARRANTS, the "TREASURY STOCK" method ASSUMES proceeds FROM exercise are USED to REPURCHASE shares at the AVERAGE market PRICE, with ONLY the NET incremental shares ADDED to the DENOMINATOR.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Anti-Dilutive Instruments — Excluded From the Calculation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Only dilutive instruments are included</div><div class="text-supporting">POTENTIAL ordinary SHARES are INCLUDED in the DILUTED EPS calculation ONLY if THEIR effect would be DILUTIVE (DECREASING EPS or INCREASING loss per SHARE) — INSTRUMENTS whose CONVERSION would be ANTI-dilutive (INCREASING EPS) are EXCLUDED entirely FROM the diluted EPS CALCULATION.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Calculating Basic EPS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Profit divided by weighted average shares</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A straightforward basic EPS calculation</div><div class="wk-body">A company reports profit attributable to ordinary shareholders of RMB 120,000,000, with a weighted average of 60,000,000 ordinary shares outstanding during the year.</div><div class="wk-answer">Basic EPS = RMB 120,000,000 ÷ 60,000,000 = <strong>RMB 2.00 per share</strong>.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Calculating Diluted EPS With Convertible Bonds</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Applying the if-converted method</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Convertible bonds outstanding</div><div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example, the company also has convertible bonds outstanding that would, if converted, add 8,000,000 shares. After-tax interest saved on conversion would be RMB 6,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">Diluted EPS = (RMB 120,000,000 + RMB 6,000,000) ÷ (60,000,000 + 8,000,000) = RMB 126,000,000 ÷ 68,000,000 = <strong>RMB 1.85 per share</strong> — LOWER than basic EPS, CONFIRMING the CONVERSION is genuinely DILUTIVE.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 34 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Basic and diluted EPS, presented on the face of the Income Statement</span><span>Reconciliation of the numerator and denominator used in basic and diluted EPS calculations</span><span>Instruments that could potentially dilute EPS in the future but were excluded as anti-dilutive</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a potential ordinary share is genuinely dilutive or anti-dilutive</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Average market price of shares, underlying the treasury stock method</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 33</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 34 vs IAS 33</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 34</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 33</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Basic/diluted EPS structure</span><span>Same methodology</span><span>Same methodology — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>If-converted/treasury stock methods</span><span>Same approach</span><span>Same approach — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard, WITH no meaningful SUBSTANTIVE divergence to REPORT.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every EPS event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Basic and diluted EPS</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Presented on the face of the Income Statement</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 11</span><span>Share-based Payment — relevant for identifying potential ordinary shares arising from employee equity awards</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Diluted EPS</div><div class="glossary-def">An EPS measure adjusting for the potential dilutive effect of convertible instruments, options, and warrants, representing the lowest possible EPS figure.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Anti-dilutive instrument</div><div class="glossary-def">A potential ordinary share whose conversion or exercise would increase EPS (or decrease loss per share), excluded from the diluted EPS calculation.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe34 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
